  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0217 database is a comprehensive library management system that includes various tables to manage books, authors, categories, and stores. The database is designed to store information about books, authors, categories, and stores, as well as user information, applications, and reviews.\nThe admin table contains information about the database administrator, including their username and password.\nThe school table contains information about the schools that are associated with the library, including their name, email, principal's first and last name, city, address, and phone number.\nThe user table contains information about the users of the library, including their username, password, first and last name, birth date, status, active borrowings, role, school name, and active reservations.\nThe book table contains information about the books in the library, including their ISBN, title, summary, publisher, page number, language, and image.\nThe category table contains information about the categories of books in the library, including their category name.\nThe book_category table contains information about the relationship between books and categories, including the category ID and the ISBN of the book.\nThe author table contains information about the authors of the books in the library, including their author name.\nThe book_author table contains information about the relationship between books and authors, including the author ID and the ISBN of the book.\nThe key_words table contains information about the keywords associated with the books in the library, including the word and the ISBN of the book.\nThe stores table contains information about the stores in the library, including the school ID, ISBN, available copies, and the relationship between the school and the book.\nThe applications table contains information about the applications made by users to borrow books, including the application ID, user ID, ISBN, start date, expiration date, status, and the relationship between the user and the book.\nThe review table contains information about the reviews left by users about the books in the library, including the ISBN, user ID, evaluation, like scale, approval status, review date, and the relationship between the user and the book.\nThe database is designed to ensure data integrity through the use of primary keys, foreign keys, and unique constraints. The primary keys ensure that each table has a unique identifier, while the foreign keys establish relationships between tables. The unique constraints ensure that each book, author, and category has a unique name. The data types of the columns are also carefully chosen to ensure that the data is accurate and consistent.",
  "gold_question": "School Library Management System \n\n1) Background / Context\n\nThe project involves developing a School Library Management System for public schools to streamline library operations. The system will facilitate the management of library resources, ensuring that technological needs for efficient library management are met.\n\n2) Objectives\n\n- Establish a centralized system for managing school libraries.\n- Enable efficient registration and administration of books and user information.\n- Facilitate borrowing, returning, and reserving books.\n- Allow user review and rating of books.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Network School Library Administrator: Manages schools, appoints library operators, and handles database management.\n- School Library Operator: Manages book data, user approvals, and supervises borrowing activities.\n- Students and Teachers: Register, view, and borrow books, make reservations, and submit reviews.\n\n4) Functional Descriptions\n\n- School Management: Register each school with details including name, contact information, and key personnel.\n- Book Management: Maintain comprehensive details about each book—title, publisher, authors, category, etc.\n- User Roles & Authentication:\n  - Admins register and approve library operators.\n  - Operators manage library operations and user interactions.\n  - Students and teachers register, view, borrow, and review books.\n- Borrowing & Reservations:\n  - Students: Borrow up to 2 books/week.\n  - Teachers: Borrow up to 1 book/week.\n  - Reservations are limited by borrowing capacity and expire after 1 week if not fulfilled.\n- Reviews & Ratings: Users can submit reviews and ratings which need approval from library operators.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Ensure secure user authentication and authorization processes.\n- Support robust data management, including backups and restorations.\n- Facilitate user-friendly interface for all functionalities.\n- Scale to manage multiple public school libraries efficiently.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_codellama13b/0217.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0217\nCREATE TABLE `admin` (\n  `admin_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`admin_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `school` (\n  `school_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `principal_first_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `principal_last_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `city` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`school_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `first_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `birth_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `active_borrowings` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `school_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `active_reservations` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`school_id`) REFERENCES `school` (`school_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `book` (\n  `isbn` varchar(13) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `summary` text NOT NULL,\n  `publisher` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `page_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `language` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `image` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`isbn`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `category` (\n  `category_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `category_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`category_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `book_category` (\n  `book_isbn` varchar(13) NOT NULL,\n  `category_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`book_isbn`, `category_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `book_category_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`book_isbn`) REFERENCES `book` (`isbn`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `book_category_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`category_id`) REFERENCES `category` (`category_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `author` (\n  `author_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `author_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`author_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `book_author` (\n  `book_isbn` varchar(13) NOT NULL,\n  `author_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`book_isbn`, `author_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `book_author_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`book_isbn`) REFERENCES `book` (`isbn`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `book_author_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`author_id`) REFERENCES `author` (`author_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `key_words` (\n  `word_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `word` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `book_isbn` varchar(13) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`word_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `key_words_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`book_isbn`) REFERENCES `book` (`isbn`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `stores` (\n  `store_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `school_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `book_isbn` varchar(13) NOT NULL,\n  `available_copies` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`store_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `stores_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`school_id`) REFERENCES `school` (`school_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `stores_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`book_isbn`) REFERENCES `book` (`isbn`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `applications` (\n  `application_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `book_isbn` varchar(13) NOT NULL,\n  `start_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `expiration_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`application_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `applications_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `applications_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`book_isbn`) REFERENCES `book` (`isbn`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `review` (\n  `review_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `book_isbn` varchar(13) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `evaluation` text NOT NULL,\n  `like_scale` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `approval_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `review_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`review_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `review_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`book_isbn`) REFERENCES `book` (`isbn`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `review_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
